From c1301005eaeafb3b5186674de31e4e5f0c28659e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:14:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging(v2): structure native coin-statistics accounting
 failures

Keep native paid-lifetime/expiry failure checks and return paths unchanged.
Log the real transaction ID for accepted-undo inconsistency, and the full
uint32 native format version as a registered numeric field. This does not
add a database migration, alter format2, or change accepted accounting.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0, reviewed exact argument catalog):
  /private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/coinstats-v2-diagnostics.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/coinstats-v2-207-apply.json --apply
  git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/index/coinstatsindex.cpp src/test/coinstatsindex_tests.cpp

The manual actual-index fixture uses the existing V2 TestAccess friend,
without extending production visibility. It corrupts an in-memory MuHash
value, removes the accounting marker from a nonempty index, and supplies
UINT32_MAX as an unsupported version, checking real CustomInit false returns,
unchanged text and typed JSON after Flush. It restores known format2 and
checks success. The accepted-undo failure remains equivalence-reviewed but
not newly injected by this fixture. Test assertions stay on the test thread.

Tier: V2 only. Place after original native coin-statistics owner
3c491043cec867e5f00beac01027c9a83023ca5f (Original-Patch v2/030), and after the
shared coinstats event conversion/adapters. Shared tests remain inherited;
this fixture additionally observes the shared corrupt-state branch.

Validation at commit: event lint415 production sites and whitespace pass.
New native cases pending; first194 immutable actual proof remains unchanged.
No public API or registry changes.
